          "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "An LD39200PU33R LDO, fed from the 5 V rail, produces 3V3 for \"MCUs and Sensors\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "As represented, the regulator does not power either MCU's VDD pins, leaving both processors without their required supply; the distinct 3.3 V net names also leave the regulator output and the +3V3 distribution unconnected.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["FCC1", "UART3_FCC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.48", "FCC1.73", "UART3_FCC1.3", "UART3_FCC1.4"],
      "nets": ["UART3_TX_FCC", "UART3_RX_FCC"],
      "observed": "The UART3_TX_FCC net contains FCC1 pin 48 (VCAP) and UART3_FCC1 pin 3; UART3_RX_FCC contains FCC1 pin 73 (VCAP) and UART3_FCC1 pin 4.",
      "expected": "The MCU's VCAP pins should be decoupled as required by the STM32H753 and should not be used as UART signals or routed to the UART connector. UART3 signals should connect to MCU UART-capable GPIO pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")"
